commit 959fab2d02ed47b39a55aaff9e6e1697b94c5268
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 02:18:55 2026 +0200

    pretrain: self-chain preemptable runs instead of --requeue
    
    Clariden sets MaxBatchRequeue=5 and a preemption spends one, so a
    --requeue'd 21-node run on `preemptable` is HELD on its sixth and
    reported as a launch failure even when all five attempts ended in clean
    preemptions. Three runs stopped that way on 2026-09-21; the cap is
    cluster-wide and admin-only, and `scontrol update Restarts=` is refused.
    
    launch_trainings.py --partition preemptable now exports PRETRAIN_CHAIN=1
    and tags the job --comment=selfchain instead of passing --requeue, and
    the wrapper queues a --dependency=singleton successor BEFORE training
    starts -- the shape data/submit_build_one.sh has always used, which sacct
    shows carried build-a-L8-165b across 29 links (24 PREEMPTED, 3 FAILED,
    1 CANCELLED, 1 COMPLETED). Each link is a new jobid, so no requeue cap
    applies, and queuing up front keeps the queue position a resubmit would
    forfeit.
    
    Five stop conditions, because a chain that cannot stop is worse than a
    requeue that gets held: `done` (cancels the pending successor), `corrupt`
    (matching the launcher's own refusal), no checkpoint progress for
    CHAIN_MAX_STALLS links, a progress count that cannot be recorded, and
    CHAIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS as a backstop. Both counters live beside this job's
    StdOut as the controller reports it, never a hard-coded path, and the
    progress file is per-user: these trees are shared, and a file a
    collaborator creates is one this user can neither rewrite nor remove.
    The no-progress guard is the one that matters -- lm-1B-L2-shallow-seed1904
    burned 14 links x 21 nodes retrying a deterministic PermissionError on
    rank 83 that Slurm still recorded as COMPLETED 0:0.
    
    pretrain_progress.py gains --cell-action, printing the word and the
    latest valid iteration so the wrapper reads a verdict rather than an exit
    status an ImportError could forge. preempt_drain.sh's safety gate now
    accepts Comment=selfchain or legacy Requeue=1 and still fails closed when
    squeue says nothing.
    
    Verified: every stop condition fires, including read-only progress file,
    read-only log dir and malformed state; the counter resets on a new valid
    checkpoint; the StdOut derivation matches live `scontrol show job`; the
    drainer gate's truth table against live jobs; every running chained job
    holds exactly one pending successor at the right node count;
    launch_trainings.py stays idempotent against those successors.

